00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.920 line:84%
That's we'll only
do some of that.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.160 line:84%
But let's talk about "Marvel's
Jessica Jones" Season Three.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.880 line:84%
 Yeah, so much
happening. with Jessica.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.070 line:84%
Got her mom resurfacing,
Trish exploring

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.100 line:84%
what it's like to have powers
of her own kind of sort,

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.600 line:84%
and of course big drama
Jerry battling ALS.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:09.860 line:84%
 Yeah, and that's
just where we're

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:11.200 line:90%
going to pick up season three.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:14.697 line:84%
I mean season two was jam
packed and so emotional.

00:04:14.697 --> 00:04:16.130 line:84%
So I'm really excited
to see what happened.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:19.279 line:84%
 Yes they were put through
the wringers of emotion

00:04:19.279 --> 00:04:20.660 line:84%
and trials and
tribulations, coming

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.750 line:90%
out looking better and worse.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:22.550 line:90%
Who knows?

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:23.460 line:84%
Because now season
three's coming.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:24.800 line:84%
But listen, I really
love they built out

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:25.790 line:90%
that whole world that season.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:26.760 line:90%
It was really, really cool.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:29.390 line:84%
 Well, you know, speaking of
being immersed in Jessica's

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:31.650 line:90%
world, I got to tour the set.

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:33.020 line:84%
 Woo.
That's nice.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:33.970 line:90%
Let's take a look around.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:34.770 line:90%
 Yeah.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.240 line:84%
 Hey, Marvelites, I am
here on the set of "Marvel's

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:42.250 line:90%
Jessica Jones" Season Three.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:46.060 line:84%
And I'm actually on a soundstage
in Brooklyn, New York.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:48.910 line:84%
A lot of people might not
realize that a lot of the sets

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:53.020 line:84%
are actually built completely
originally here in a studio.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.280 line:84%
And I'm going to take you
inside for a little set tour.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:56.080 line:90%
Come on.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:02.290 line:90%
And now, I am on the set.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.050 line:90%
This is Jessica's elevator.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:05.980 line:84%
Of course, it's not an
elevator in real life

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:08.050 line:84%
because there is a solid
floor underneath us.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:10.750 line:84%
But you might remember a
lot of dramatic moments

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:13.800 line:84%
and awkward moments
shared in this elevator.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:14.700 line:90%
 You want to go

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.050 line:90%
to a movie sometime?

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.390 line:90%
 This is Malcolm's apartment.

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:20.140 line:90%
[KNOCKING]

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:21.460 line:90%
I don't think he's home.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.130 line:84%
He's probably entertaining
a lady friend.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:27.820 line:84%
But this is, of course,
Jessica Jones' assistant,

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.280 line:84%
well, on again, off
again, on again,

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:33.340 line:84%
off again, on again,
off, it's complicated.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:34.750 line:90%
But let's see if Jessica's home.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.800 line:84%
Here we are in Jessica
Jones's bedroom.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.630 line:84%
There have been a lot
of special moments

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:44.840 line:84%
in this room and a lot
of drama, not only did

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:47.990 line:84%
sparks fly between
Jessica and Luke Cage,

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.780 line:84%
this is also the place where
Luke was brought when he had

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.520 line:84%
a traumatic brain
injury and Claire

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.320 line:90%
Temple had to save his life.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.570 line:84%
There are also of course
were sparks between her

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:58.220 line:90%
and Oscar, her super.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:05:59.900 line:84%
But there was also
a beautiful moment

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:02.300 line:84%
that she shared with her mom
where they laid right here

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:06.170 line:84%
and slept, for the first
time together in 17 years.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.510 line:84%
And one of my favorite things
about being in this room

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:11.610 line:84%
is, I definitely saw some
coconut body wash over there.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:14.420 line:84%
So now we all know what
Jessica Jones smells like.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:15.680 line:90%
Let's see what else I can find.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.450 line:84%
And here we are in
Jessica's kitchen.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:25.010 line:84%
OK, she's not necessarily
the best cook.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.930 line:90%
But she does have dishes.

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:29.960 line:84%
And I mean, I do
sort of love this set

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:32.780 line:84%
because it's all built
like a real cold water

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.280 line:90%
tenement in the old days.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:37.730 line:84%
You've got exposed pipes
and all kinds of fun, funky

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.740 line:84%
little details,
right down to a bunch

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:41.480 line:90%
of leftover coffee in the sink.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.010 line:90%
I mean, relatable.

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:43.810 line:90%
Let's see what else.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:50.840 line:84%
And here we are in
Jessica's living room.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.540 line:84%
And by living room, I mean this
is how she makes her living

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:55.610 line:90%
for Alias Investigations.

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:58.140 line:84%
This is where she does
all of her research,

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:01.340 line:84%
whether it's finding out
where Kilgrave has been hiding

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:05.540 line:84%
or what IGH is up to and how
she got her super powers.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:09.530 line:84%
And it looks like it's been
through some rough times

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:10.850 line:90%
with these gouges.

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:13.010 line:84%
But you know, when
she's looking for clues,

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:15.860 line:84%
there's only one way you can
really string together a theory

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:18.830 line:84%
and that's by putting
them all up on the board.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:21.380 line:84%
I guess sometimes that
can be frustrating,

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:26.480 line:84%
if this big punch hole in this
board is to tell us anything.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:28.730 line:84%
But I'm going to be
looking for even more clues

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:31.940 line:84%
about "Marvel's Jessica
Jones" Season Three.

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:35.360 line:84%
You should check it out
streaming only on Netflix.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:37.980 line:84%
And for now, I'm just going
to kind of hang out with Jess.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.630 line:84%
I'm going to see if
she comes home later.

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:40.430 line:90%
Bye, bye.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.690 line:84%
 Whoa, I thought that
was an apartment building.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:45.630 line:90%
That's a set.

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:46.430 line:90%
 Yeah.

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:47.370 line:90%
Isn't that crazy?

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.190 line:84%
It's a whole floor
of an apartment.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:50.020 line:90%
Jess lives there.

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:50.820 line:90%
Malcolm lives there.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.070 line:90%
It's like it feels like home.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:53.220 line:84%
 Is it home?
Did you move in?

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:54.020 line:90%
 I did.

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:55.040 line:90%
I live there.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:55.840 line:90%
 Yeah.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:56.715 line:90%
How much is the rent?

00:07:56.715 --> 00:07:59.230 line:90%
 It's uh, I'm squatting.

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:00.030 line:90%
It's fine.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.310 line:90%
 Is there running water?

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:03.170 line:84%
Yeah, well there is a lot
more to come this season,

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.670 line:84%
including a new character
that will be a very

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:05.990 line:90%
interesting foil for Jessica.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:08.330 line:84%
 Yeah in fact, I caught up
with that mysterious character

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:10.490 line:84%
played by the incredibly
fun Benjamin Walker

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:12.250 line:84%
when I was hanging out
at Jessica's place.

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:13.990 line:90%
 Oh, dope, here it is.

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:16.500 line:10%
 I am hanging out here on the
set of "Marvel's Jessica Jones"

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:18.000 line:10%
Season Three.
And look who I found.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.550 line:10%
It's Ben Walker.
Hello.

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:20.760 line:10%
 Hello.
Hello.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:21.560 line:10%
 Hello.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.280 line:84%
So what can you tell us about
your character, Erik Gelden.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:29.240 line:84%
 Not a lot, but enough
to keep him interesting.

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:35.000 line:10%
He is a blackmailer,
a gambler, a drinker.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.840 line:10%
He has moved to New
York from the South

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:42.200 line:10%
for some family and
personal reasons.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:46.910 line:84%
And he's kind of found
himself in hot water, largely

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:49.490 line:90%
because of his own behavior.

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:51.800 line:84%
 Right, so that's
on, that's on Erik.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:57.350 line:84%
 Well, you meet Erik early
when he is drunk, in trouble,

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:59.360 line:90%
in pain, and desperate.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:00.500 line:90%
 That's perfect for Jessica.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:01.440 line:90%
That's like her whole thing.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.240 line:90%
 Right, exactly.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.060 line:84%
It's kind of star
crossed lovers.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.910 line:90%
And he needs her help.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:06.710 line:90%
 Right.

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:08.240 line:90%
 So that's how we meet Erik.

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:10.580 line:90%
But he has a lot to offer.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:13.580 line:84%
And I think Jessica
quickly realizes that.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:16.350 line:84%
 Now you get to of course
play opposite Krysten Ritter.

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:17.150 line:90%
 Sure.

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:19.050 line:84%
What has it been like
working with Krysten?

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:19.850 line:90%
 She's great.

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:23.090 line:84%
She's a pro on camera
and off camera.

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:24.890 line:90%
She directed an episode.

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:29.540 line:84%
So, that's been incredibly
positive, because you know,

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:33.080 line:84%
this is my first kind
of long form television.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:35.810 line:84%
And to kind of have her
holding my hand through it

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:37.210 line:90%
has been really great.

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:39.700 line:84%
It's kind of like, (WHISPERING)
Ben, stand over there

